From c0b6a4c5d0b90db5b8d35dc7b7fddef176a12d8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 10:40:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 06/15] rdna-boosts: block 06: MMB quantized prefill GEMM

Re-based onto a691b2345.  Applied clean, but its routed path called the pre-re-base
`ggml_cuda_launch_mm_ids_helper` (which produced `expert_bounds` only).

The helper now emits upstream #31047's `tile_spec` (block 00's re-implementation), so it
gained an optional `expert_bounds` output that MMB keeps using: one compaction serves
MMQ/MMF (tile_spec) and MMB (per-expert bounds), and both MMB call sites (routed and
routed-GLU) allocate the tile_spec buffer they do not read.  No MMB kernel logic changed.

Validated: build green; MMB_DENSE fires (GGML_CUDA_MMB_LOG=1: `MMB_CFG ... dense_geom=1
routed=0 ...`, `MMB_DENSE blk.0.ffn_gate_inp.weight type=f32 M=128 K=2048 T=512`);
`GGML_CUDA_MMB=0` byte-identical (108 chars, sha d94aef3f5033) on Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B.
